      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've wanted this for a long time as well. The closest right now is turning your nameplate transparency to 0% and disabling banners allowing just the text and profile picture to show. I wish I could disable the pictures still and only have text and the visual queue for mic activity and that would be my ideal. Pre VRC+ the ideal was exactly what I had, and every update regarding UI strays further and further from what was the most usable and de cluttered interface. If I wanted declutter alone I could just turn nameplates off, but I'm wanting functional and minimal so when there's 10 overlapping nameplates on screen I can tell which nametag is actually lighting up to know who's speaking. For anyone playing with low volume or earmuffs on, any sort of hearing impairment, this would be a huge improvment.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-08-11T09:41:09.036Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Right now we can chose between shown, icon only or hidden:\n\n-Shown is too much, it's like a whole billboard of mostly useless visual clutter, it almost completely covers the top half of the visual field in crowded instances.\n\n-Icon only is mostly useless because most people either don't set one or change it all the time so it's not a reliable identifier.\n\n-Hidden is confusing because some people change avis all the time.\n\nI want the option to just display the username, and nothing else.\n\nThis is as much needed as an accessibility feature for some as it is simply a practical way to keep our visual field clean and readable in VR for everyone.\n\nI know this request has been denied already 6 years ago but without providing clear justification, only mentioning an \"ealrier post\" now lost to time. The landscape is changing and it feels like it needs to be adressed again as the UI and nameplates are being reworked again.",
